  "contract": [
    "NewWindowsObserver requires an explicit profile and performs no I/O. The default Windows Observe still refuses without that profile.",
    "The profile bounds source age, rate error, and additional UTC uncertainty. One W32Time status binds the last synchronization timestamp and elapsed age in 100ns units. Source drift includes timestamp precision and quantization.",
    "Unsafe synchronization, leap, stratum, source flags, malformed timestamps, overflow, and excessive combined error return no usable time.",
    "The native reader uses a local anonymous pipe and query-only service handles. It checks the pipe server PID against the running W32Time process before RPC and retains a process handle for its completion check.",
    "A fixed stream, disabled DNS resolver, fragment/reply limits, and deadline clamps bound QueryStatus transport. No application credential is selected.",
    "At most one native service-manager call remains outstanding. Caller cancellation returns while an uninterruptible native call retains its slot until cleanup.",
    "CI will start the existing W32Time service on disposable Windows runners and require real pipe/status tests. Application code starts no service or time synchronization."
  ],
